                                <tr>
                <td bgcolor="#f0f0f0" width="20%" valign="top"><b>Developer Testing Note:</b></td>
                <td id="customfield_10038-66005-value" class="value" bgcolor="#ffffff" width="80%">      <p>Need to test with campaigns which include specific domain and default domain. </p>

<p>Need to test with both <tt>disable_domain_split</tt> turned on and turned off. This is done by mongo so please ask programmer to update for account.</p>
  </td>
            </tr>
                                <tr>
                <td bgcolor="#f0f0f0" width="20%" valign="top"><b>QA Test Plan:</b></td>
                <td id="customfield_10039-66005-value" class="value" bgcolor="#ffffff" width="80%">      <p><a href="https://ongage.atlassian.net/browse/RND-7172" title="smart-link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://ongage.atlassian.net/browse/RND-7172</a> </p>

<p><b>QA Test Plan</b></p>

<p><b>Scope</b><br/>
Verify that the campaign picks the expected number of eligible contacts according to the configured quota for the configured Domain, with disable_domain_split set to ON/OFF both.</p>

<p><b>Out of Scope</b><br/>
There is no need to test other campaign functionalities unrelated to contact pickup count, quota behavior, and domain split configuration.</p>

<p><b>Test Cases</b><br/>
Case 1:<br/>
Step 1: Ask the developer to enable the disable_domain_split flag ON.<br/>
Step 2: Once the developer turn ON this flag, run a campaign using a segment containing 20 Gmail domain email IDs and 20 other domain email IDs. Use quota in it<br/>
Step 3: Verify that eligible contacts are not unexpectedly excluded due to quota limitations.</p>

<p>Once case 1 is verified then perform case 2</p>

<p><b>Case 2:</b> <br/>
Step 1: Ask the developer to enable the disable_domain_split flag OFF.<br/>
Step 2: Once the developer turn OFF this flag, run a campaign using a segment containing 20 Gmail domain email IDs and 20 other domain email IDs. Use quota in it<br/>
Step 3: Verify that eligible contacts are not unexpectedly excluded due to quota limitations.</p>

<p><b>Expected Result</b><br/>
The campaign should pick the expected number of eligible contacts according to the configured quota for the configured Domain, with disable_domain_split set to ON/OFF, without unexpected contact exclusions.</p>

<p>Environment: <b>Lab / Production</b></p>

<p><b>Exit Criteria:</b> Successfully verify that the campaign picks the expected eligible contacts according to the configured quota in all planned scenarios.</p>
  </td>
            </tr>
            </table>

    <br/>

    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
