        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-90971"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>This is the split from my end</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>┌─total─┬─gmail─┬─non_gmail─┬─connection_id─┐
│  5000 │  2998 │      2002 │       1094951 │
│  5001 │   562 │      4439 │       1094419 │
│  5001 │  2999 │      2002 │       1094968 │
│  5001 │     0 │      5001 │       1094969 │
│  8002 │     0 │      8002 │       1094404 │
│  5001 │  3000 │      2001 │       1094967 │
│  5002 │  2998 │      2004 │       1094955 │
│  4999 │  3000 │      1999 │       1094954 │
│  5001 │     0 │      5001 │       1094966 │
│  5002 │  3000 │      2002 │       1094880 │
└───────┴───────┴───────────┴───────────────┘</pre>
</div></div>

<hr />

<p>segment 1207913149 had 105438 in <a href="http://gmail.com" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">gmail.com</a> and 42337 in all other domains</p>

<p>segment 1207836312 had 76450 in <a href="http://gmail.com" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">gmail.com</a> and 34816 in all other domains</p>

<p>all 181888 emails were unique and there were no duplicates for <a href="http://gmail.com" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">gmail.com</a></p>

<p>all 77153 email were unique and there were no duplicates for other domains</p>

<hr />

<p>I think I understand the problem. it looks like the default quota takes into consideration the <a href="http://gmail.com" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">gmail.com</a> quota.</p>

<p>In the UI it suggests that the default quota should be added to the <a href="http://gmail.com" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">gmail.com</a> quota</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-91004"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="557058:eab77149-8147-4063-8343-0349dd4c4e88"
